{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"FINAL DEBUG / COMPLETION REPORT (2026-08-14)\n\nProblem: five invariant Git/rebar fixture topologies were rebuilt from scratch for every consumer, contributing 103.416 measured worker-seconds across the top five modules in organic Verify run 31846417650.\n\nProven root cause: the function-scoped builders in test_secret_screen_e7a9.py, test_list_filters.py, test_concurrency_regression.py/test_b636_rebuild_history_loss.py, test_prepare_reclaim_backup.py, and test_inline_write_push.py performed repeated repository initialization and fixed topology population even though each asserted behavior begins from an equivalent post-setup state. Focused runtime probes separated setup from call work and measured real-build versus isolated-copy ratios of approximately 12x, 17.7x, 23x, 13.8x, and 15.7x.\n\nProof and OSS legitimacy: runtime mutation/isolation probes rejected test-body cost and unavoidable fresh-state semantics. Django setUpTestData/deep-copy plus rollback, Rails fixture loading plus rollback/cache invalidation, GitLab let_it_be/prepared repositories plus rollback/reload, and pytest tmp_path_factory all use the same expensive-template plus per-test-isolation practice, while retaining from-scratch cases where copying is not faithful. Tracker precedents peculiar-calmy-bubblefish and adored-duskish-kissingbug accepted and hardened this pattern; no rejection was found.\n\nTests and repair proof: commit 3bf9b2b2c41f00f76ee4c5298e185ab95e4269fb added/extended behavioral sentinels in tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py and migrated only proven-equivalent fixtures. The op-cert key defect was observed RED with identical template/A/B private-key digests, GREEN after copied .opcert-key/.pub removal and lazy reminting, and RED again when the exact defect was reintroduced. The object-alternates sentinel was RED before the fail-fast guard and GREEN afterward. Existing sentinels cover half-rewritten and bare worktree pointers, source-path leakage, shared refs/object stores, identity/signing isolation, restrictive key mode, virgin templates, sibling remotes, gate snapshots, caches, and mutable config. They assert observable Git/rebar behavior, not implementation text.\n\nFix: each pytest worker now builds five invariant templates once, then makes and repairs a complete isolated copy per test. Direct initialization/recovery contracts remain from-scratch. No production behavior or dependency changed. No test, assertion, selector, mutation shard, Python cell, or platform was removed, skipped, sampled, xfailed, or weakened. The merged diff added 591 lines and removed 103, predominantly reusable topology repair plus isolation contracts.\n\nScope and safety: all 125 affected tests passed in 46.95s. The exact local default selector passed 13,441 tests with 17 expected skips in 1,254.00s; the exact integration selector passed 167 with 2 skips in 114.59s. make check passed Ruff, format, complexity, DCO, workflow guards, and mypy. The local selectors used pytest automatic basetemps (no --basetemp override); their numbered temporary roots were not logged and were later pruned, so no retained-size claim is made.\n\nOriginal-report replication: Gerrit 1799 patchset 1 passed LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 and merged as 3bf9b2b2c4. Its macOS log contained zero >1s fixture_setup spans from the five migrated modules; the previous organic run measured 103.416s in those modules. The only individual test above 20s was the separately owned 3,000-ticket/3,000-comment import benchmark at 21.05s. This proves the targeted repeated-setup mechanism is gone without claiming that all suite growth is solved.\n\nCI_RESULT: {\"run_id\":\"31854708530\",\"status\":\"passed\",\"duration\":1857,\"fixes_applied\":[],\"retry_count\":0}. End-to-end was 30m57s; macOS was 29m22s, comprising 25m30s default, 2m04s integration, and 1m48s setup/teardown. Ubuntu py3.11/3.12/3.13 jobs were 8m53s/9m59s/11m42s. The preceding organic run 31846417650 was 29m47s end-to-end, so this single noisy full-run pair does not demonstrate a wall-clock reduction; the causal evidence is the paired setup probes and disappearance of the targeted >1s spans. Fresh runs must determine the average.\n\nSiblings: the five confirmed equivalent fixture families were repaired in scope. Initialization/recovery fixtures were intentionally excluded. No missing parallel surface exists because clone_topology_template is test infrastructure consumed only by these fixtures.\n\nResidual risk and prevention: the import benchmark remains an individual contention long pole under ravenous-beribboned-walleye; its standalone behavior and accepted 3,000-record contract are not weakened here. A local 87.27s bare-pytest import-convention outlier reproduced standalone in 4.23s, classifying it as contention rather than intrinsic test work. Continued post-merge sampling is required before declaring the 20-30 minute average goal achieved.\n\nBack-out: revert 3bf9b2b2c4 to restore per-test from-scratch fixture construction; no production behavior or coverage destination depends on the optimization."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786761044367353001,"uuid":"44e928e1-fbc0-4f1b-b849-e4939a65a492"}